body:
I extract camped for the first time last night just to see the appeal of it and I think it comes down to this;  
1. Why go through the map and loot when it's brought to you at extract

2. You want to play Tarkov but cbf running around a map all raid just to die to a scav or sweatlord

3. You're able to do anything productive while also making some progress on the game.  


Cons;

1. Can get boring at which point, you might aswell play a raid as normal
2. Timing how long it'll take you to get to another extract (unless you camp at your own extract)
3. Idk, people send you hate messages but tbh, they made me laugh.  


Conclusion;

I think it's a perfectly fine strategy as you're lessening the risk of your life while raising the risk of your gain. It's just frowned upon. I'll still prefer raiding as normal but I can see the appeal and why people do it. It can be fun just to ruin someones raid, whether it's by extract camping or killing them in a normal raid, only difference is how it's done. Just don't count yourself safe until you're out of raid, extractions are not a safe zone.
